.TH auto-nfs-server-setup 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-nfs-server-setup - Configure a host as an NFS server

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-nfs-server-setup 'allowed-clients' sysctl|daemon domain
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
'allowed-clients'   Network spec for clients allowed to connect
sysctl|daemon       Select a method to map usernames across client/server
domain              Domain for nfsuserd if using daemon for mapping
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-nfs-server-setup
command configures a host as an NFS server.

The 'allowed-clients' argument is a list of IPs,  hostnames, and/or
ranges that may include CIDR or separate network and mask notations.
Enclose it in single quotes if it contains any whitespace, so
that it is seen as a single argument.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-nfs-server-setup -network=192.168.0.0/24 sysctl
auto-nfs-server-setup '-network=192.168.0.0 -mask=255.255.255.0' sysctl
auto-nfs-server-setup 'bobspc.local julie.laptop.local' daemon our.domain
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/etc/exports
/etc/zfs/exports
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), nfsd(8), nfsuserd(8), rpc.statd(8), rpc.lockd(8)

